    {
        "content": "<p>If nobody is working on it I can deal with <code>Function.leftLim/rightLim</code>.</p>",
        "id": 622240977,
        "sender_full_name": "Etienne Marion",
        "timestamp": 1788776185
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You should be able to get the automatic name translation to work if you add this to the <code>abbreviationDict</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"leftColim\"</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"rightLim\"</span><span class=\"o\">),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"rightColim\"</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"leftLim\"</span><span class=\"o\">),</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Because otherwise the name <code>leftLim</code> is translated to <code>leftColim</code></p>\n<p>This is analogous to the approach with <code>IsSuccLimit</code>/<code>IsPredLimit</code>.</p>",
        "id": 622243103,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1788776871
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It works indeed, thanks!</p>",
        "id": 622356902,
        "sender_full_name": "Etienne Marion",
        "timestamp": 1788808892
    },
